<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bustan al-Salatin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1638</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bustan al-Salatin, 'Garden of Kings', is a Malay encyclopaedic work written by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuruddin-ar-raniri">Nuruddin ar-Raniri</a> at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a>, begun in 1638 at the command of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iskandar-thani">Iskandar Thani</a>. In seven books it covers the creation of the world, the prophets, the history of kings in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> and the Malay world, and advice on good government. It is one of the largest works of classical Malay literature.</p></div>
